      "review_markdown": "The new route-driven inspiration source is not aligned with the still-stale skin predicate in the left panel, so the TTI panel can render mismatched AIPC/Cloud halves during probe transitions. That is a user-visible regression introduced by this change.\n\nReview comment:\n\n- [P2] Keep the TTI skin and inspiration source on the same route — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\src\\view\\text_to_image\\text_to_image_right_content_page.dart:175-182\n  When `useAipcInspirationsProvider` flips to true, this page now switches to the local AIPC catalog immediately, but `TextToImageLibrarayPanel.buildColumnInLowerLayer()` still decides the surrounding skin with the older `supportsAipcTti` check (`text_to_image_left_panel.dart:357`). On startup or after a probe failure that leaves the support flag false, that splits the panel into an AIPC inspiration list inside the Full Features chrome until some other rebuild happens, which is a visible mixed-mode regression.\n",
      "head_commit_message": null
    },
