        "failed_tests": [],
        "dart_diff_coverage": {
          "percent": 77,
          "num_lines": 489,
          "num_violations": 110
        },
        "cpp_diff_coverage": null
      },
      "review_markdown": "The patch introduces regressions in the new Iris auth/credit flow: anonymous Essential sends can reuse a stale member token, unsigned 365 users are misclassified as out-of-credit instead of needing re-login, and dismissed post-review sign-in dialogs suppress the recovery UI. Those are user-visible behavioral breaks rather than harmless refactors.\n\nFull review comments:\n\n- [P1] Preserve the UUID on the anonymous Essential credential path — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\agent_studio\\test_page\\controller\\agent_chat_controller.dart:264-266\n  When an Essential user has a stale `giMemberToken` but no validated login, this branch still passes that token into `selectCredentials()`, and `selectCredentials()` will prefer it over `deviceUuid`. That means the supposed free-trial UUID path can silently send `member_token` instead of the anonymous identity and fail the Iris request. See `lib/agent_studio/test_page/controller/agent_chat_controller.dart:257-266`.\n\n- [P1] Keep unsigned 365 users on the re-login path — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\agent_studio\\test_page\\service\\agent_generation_credit_preflight.dart:309-317\n  This new guard classifies every send with no validated sign-in and no raw member credential as `creditNotEnough`. For a 365 user who is simply signed out, that is the normal pre-send state, but they should still be routed to `needReLogin` rather than being told they lack credits. As written, unsigned paid users will never get the login prompt. See `lib/agent_studio/test_page/service/agent_generation_credit_preflight.dart:309-317`.\n\n- [P2] Re-check sign-in success before skipping credit recovery — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\agent_studio\\test_page\\controller\\iris_sign_in_gate.dart:93-95\n  If the sign-in dialog is opened and then dismissed, `_defaultPostReviewAuthorize()` still returns `signInHandled` because it only records that the dialog was presented. `AgentEventMixin._showPostReviewCreditRecovery()` treats that as terminal and returns without showing the credit POU, so users who close the login window lose the recovery flow entirely. See `lib/agent_studio/test_page/controller/iris_sign_in_gate.dart:93-95`.\n",
      "head_commit_message": null
    },
