        "failed_tests": [],
        "dart_diff_coverage": null,
        "cpp_diff_coverage": null
      },
      "review_markdown": "The new frame heartbeat under-reports slow and janky frames because it truncates timing values to whole milliseconds before comparing them to the thresholds. That changes the diagnostic output for a real subset of frame timings, so the patch is not fully correct.\n\nReview comment:\n\n- [P2] Compare frame durations with sub-millisecond precision — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\src\\utility\\frame_heartbeat.dart:89-92\n  Using `Duration.inMilliseconds` truncates fractional milliseconds, so frames that are just over a threshold (for example 32.1ms or 100.9ms) are bucketed as if they were still under it. That makes the heartbeat systematically undercount borderline slow/janky frames in any run where timings land between integer milliseconds. See `lib/src/utility/frame_heartbeat.dart` (`tallyFrameTimings`).\n",
      "head_commit_message": null
    },
