          }
        ],
        "failed_tests": [],
        "dart_diff_coverage": {
          "percent": 100,
          "num_lines": 61,
          "num_violations": 0
        },
        "cpp_diff_coverage": null
      },
      "review_markdown": "The new feature-page gate can misclassify a request as abandoned when the first snapshot is taken before the provider hub is ready, because the null-to-real transition is treated as a page change. That can silently drop a valid generate in the exact startup/unwired scenario the helper claims to support.\n\nReview comment:\n\n- [P2] Treat unknown page snapshots as unchanged — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\src\\controller\\aipc_module\\aipc_feature_page_presence.dart:81-82\n  When `capture()` returns `page: null` because `ProviderHub` is not wired yet, any later real snapshot will satisfy `before.page != after.page` and be classified as `abandoned`. In the startup / unit-test case this code already documents, that turns a long-running download into a silent drop even though the user never navigated away. `didLeaveFeaturePage()` should treat unknown/null snapshots as \"unchanged\" instead of a departure.\n",
      "head_commit_message": null
    },
