        "dart_diff_coverage": {
          "percent": 100,
          "num_lines": 61,
          "num_violations": 0
        },
        "cpp_diff_coverage": null
      },
      "review_markdown": "The new abandonment gate can misclassify a cold-start or otherwise unwired provider snapshot transition as user navigation, causing a valid generation to be silently dropped. That is a user-visible regression in the new logic.\n\nReview comment:\n\n- [P2] Ignore unknown page snapshots instead of treating them as abandonment — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\src\\controller\\aipc_module\\aipc_feature_page_presence.dart:82-83\n  If `ProviderHub` is not wired for the first capture but becomes ready before the second, `before.page != after.page` will return `true` and the preflight will emit `abandoned` even though the user never navigated away. That contradicts the contract in this file that unreadable snapshots should degrade to \"nothing changed\" and can silently drop a real generate on startup or any lazily initialized test harness.\n",
      "head_commit_message": null
    },
