      "review_markdown": "The patch removes the only project-load migration for rotated titles without persisted auto-line-break state, which regresses legacy project/template loading. Existing files can now open with broken title layout until a manual rotation forces re-evaluation.\n\nReview comment:\n\n- [P2] Preserve the on-load auto-wrap migration for legacy rotated titles — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\src\\controller\\promeo_template\\promeo_template_controller.dart:3045-3046\n  When loading a project/template that contains a rotated title saved before ALB state was persisted, `restoreProjectAutoLineBreak()` returns false and the removed `migrateRotatedAutoLineBreakOnLoad()` path never runs. In that scenario, the title keeps its old one-line wrap box and can clip/re-break until the user manually rotates it again. See `lib/src/controller/promeo_template/promeo_template_controller.dart` and the deleted migration path in `lib/src/model/tlobject/effect_object/template_object/tl_title_object.dart`.\n",
      "head_commit_message": null
    },
