        "cpp_diff_coverage": null
      },
      "review_markdown": "The new gallery-height helper does not type-check as written because it returns the `num` result of `clamp()` from a `double` function. That blocks the build until the return value is converted to `double`.\n\nReview comment:\n\n- [P0] Return a double from `V3GalleryBoxHeight.resolve` — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\src\\view\\magic_designer\\ai_design_generator\\v3_preview_canvas_frame.dart:148-155\n  `clamp()` returns a `num`, so `return available.clamp(0.0, cap);` does not satisfy this method’s declared `double` return type and will fail static analysis/compile as soon as the new gallery sizing helper is built. Please cast the result or use `min`/`max` so the helper type-checks. [lib/src/view/magic_designer/ai_design_generator/v3_preview_canvas_frame.dart:148-155]\n",
      "head_commit_message": null
    },
    {
