        "failed_tests": [],
        "dart_diff_coverage": {
          "percent": 80,
          "num_lines": 20,
          "num_violations": 4
        },
        "cpp_diff_coverage": null
      },
      "review_markdown": "The patch adds a re-entrancy guard, but for product background AIPC it is armed only after an earlier async preprocessing step has already started. A fast second click can still slip through that window and launch another run, so the duplicate-click bug is not fully fixed.\n\nReview comment:\n\n- [P2] Arm the AIPC guard before the async PDBG preflight — C:\\actions-runner\\_work\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo-pc-promeo\\promeo_trunk\\lib\\src\\controller\\setting_panel_controllers\\ai_tool_panel_controllers\\product_background_panel_controller.dart:1120-1121\n  If the user taps AIPC Generate again while `clickGenerateBtn()` is still awaiting `BrushMaskController().updateForegroundImageForProductBG()`, `_aipcGeneratePendingToken` has not been set yet, so `isAipcGeneratePending` still reads false and the second tap can re-enter the same flow. That leaves a duplicate-run window in `product_background_generate_by_text_panel_controller.dart`/this controller even though the new guard is meant to prevent it; move the guard to the entry point or set it before the first awaited preflight step so the whole AIPC request lifecycle is covered.\n",
      "head_commit_message": null
    }
  ],
